15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Infographic explaining how temperature influences floral sex expression and reproductive outcomes in plants. Panel A shows temperature-dependent sex expression, where low temperature favors female flowers and high temperature favors male flowers during early development. Panel B illustrates general reproductive heat injury, with heat stress at later stages causing pollen sterility, stigma dysfunction, fertilization failure, or embryo abortion, leading to reduced fertility. Panel C outlines a conceptual framework linking temperature cues through signal perception, hormonal integration, sex-determination, resulting in different floral sex fates and reproductive outcomes such as fertility and yield.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Diagram comparing temperature-dependent regulation of floral sex in cucurbits. Panel A shows cucumber-centered models where low temperature increases ethylene biosynthesis and promotes female flowers, while high temperature promotes male flowers by increasing WIP activity. Panel B illustrates epigenetic regulation, where temperature changes lead to DNA methylation changes affecting ACS activity, WIP expression, ethylene biosynthesis, and sex fate. The right section details how CmWIP1 promoter methylation and silencing in melon, caused by transposon insertion, results in gynoecy. Icons and arrows depict molecular and developmental steps with male and female floral symbols.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Illustration of a balance scale comparing stability and plasticity in sex expression under fluctuating temperatures. Stability side lists robust reproductive development, consistent floral sex ratio, stable fruit set and yield, and reduced developmental variability. Plasticity side lists responsive sex allocation, flexible adjustment to temperature, potential adaptive strategy, and short-term environmental resilience. Caption suggests an appropriate balance may enhance reproductive success across environments.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Four-panel infographic summarizes a plant science research pipeline: fundamental discovery \(temperature treatments, developmental window identification, floral sex phenotyping\), mechanistic integration \(hormone networks, sex-determination genes, epigenetic regulation, cell-type specificity\), translational tools \(natural variation, QTL/GWAS, molecular markers, gene editing, predictive models, validated targets\), and agricultural applications \(breeding, seed production and horticulture, greenhouse and field management\), with each step depicted using simple icons and subpoints.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
